{"duration_api_ms":179208,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a9c43278-d09d-46db-85b0-6cbe4ec48925","total_cost_usd":0.220706,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14153,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":16409,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":10876},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14153,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":16409,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14153,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14153},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":16409,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14153,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.220706,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":10876,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is a one-dimensional curve in flight_path_angle. It sits in the corner of the design box at bluntness 1.2, cone 70 and D about 3.35 (fluxes 241k-276k W/m2, bondline temperatures 391-411 K). Three constraints bind. max_g caps gamma near -3.57 deg. The heatshield mass fraction caps D near 3.385 m. The aero surrogate's convex hull caps bluntness and cone. Every geometry failure has bluntness >= 1.22 at cone 70, or cone 69 with bluntness 1.2. Normalised hypervolume is dominated by the temperature axis (150 K span against a 2.5e6 W/m2 flux span), so the main remaining gains are a slightly larger D at the mass limit, plus extending the front to shallow gamma.\",\"evidence\":[\"Fixed D=3.35, bluntness 1.2, cone 70, gamma swept from -2.0 to -3.45 (C-3cfec4d90b09, C-4370b59bae5e, C-e6138656a3bd, C-a51f1ded896c, C-15eefd667953): flux 241k->276k, temperature 410.7->392.9 K, g 9.72->11.79. Steeper entry lowers temperature at the cost of flux and g.\",\"Gamma -3.58, bluntness 1.2, cone 70, D swept from 3.30 to 3.38 (C-363a563b3536, C-492a26649e0e, C-764c593a20a3, C-6146d28a8413, C-2a109f1c4205, C-053e6577c074): flux falls 285.1k->275.4k (about -1.2k per 0.01 m) and temperature 392.49->391.08 K, so larger D is better on both objectives. g rises only about 0.004 per 0.01 m.\",\"Mass-fraction margin: 0.0207 at D=3.35, 0.0149 at 3.36, 0.0090 at 3.37, 0.0031 at 3.38 (C-3e5fe5688040, C-053e6577c074). That is about -0.0059 per 0.01 m, so the limit is D of about 3.385.\",\"g is close to 12.0 at C-6146d28a8413 (-3.58, D 3.35), C-3e5fe5688040 (-3.57, D 3.37) and C-c4095cf95503 (-3.5, D 3.35, 11.869). This gives about 1.66 g per deg, so at D of about 3.383 the gamma limit is roughly -3.57.\",\"Geometry failures C-35e288c12205, C-11ae4eb65bbb, C-f414065c6995, C-02c5b1aac369, C-660a8eef4199, C-f933198e1835 and C-02bec3a7a6f4 all have bluntness >= 1.22 at cone 70. C-460ff98d4dde (cone 69, bluntness 1.2) also fails. Lower bluntness or smaller D are worse: C-d883f15f56c5 (bluntness 1.05) has higher flux, and C-7139ecfe995b and C-6c8d751b6b54 (D about 1.2-1.4) have flux 1.8-2.6e6 and violate temperature.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak flux scales roughly as sqrt(rho_peak/Rn), so larger D and a larger nose radius lower it. Bondline temperature follows the integrated heat load, which a steeper entry lowers by shortening the pulse. Peak g is set mainly by gamma. The optimum therefore sits where the mass-fraction limit (D about 3.385) and the g limit (gamma about -3.57) meet, at the highest bluntness and cone angle the surrogate hull allows. This is the prior-knowledge picture, and the tabulated trends agree with it. I stay on the known-safe edge (bluntness 1.2, cone 70), and move D from 3.35 to about 3.383 to shift the whole front down in both objectives. I also sweep gamma from -1.5 to -3.565 to extend the front to low flux and to densify it, since a shallower entry trades temperature for flux.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Values at gamma shallower than -2.0 are extrapolated (about -1.5 to -1.9), so temperature and flux there may be off by several K or several percent. The D=3.384-3.385 points sit within about 0.001 of the mass-fraction limit, and the g margin at gamma -3.565 to -3.56 is only about 0.01. Either could tip a point to infeasible. The hull boundary of the aero surrogate is not known precisely, so I did not try bluntness > 1.2 or cone < 70 with bluntness 1.2. I did not test any different region of the design space, so a better basin may exist that I have no data on.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-3cfec4d90b09\",\"rationale\":\"Extend the front to the shallowest allowed entry (gamma -1.5) at the larger D=3.383 to gain low-flux coverage.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.383,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":226800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":418.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the extrapolated low-flux end of the front; it is far from any evaluated gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3cfec4d90b09\",\"rationale\":\"Fill between gamma -1.5 and -2.0 at D=3.383.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.383,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":231300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the curvature of the front for gamma shallower than -2.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3cfec4d90b09\",\"rationale\":\"Move the gamma -2.0 front point to a larger D for lower flux and temperature.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.383,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":235700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Should dominate C-3cfec4d90b09 if the D trend holds at shallow gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3cfec4d90b09\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-front point at larger D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.383,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":242500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":407.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Interpolated between -2.0 and -2.5; confirms the D benefit is uniform along the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4370b59bae5e\",\"rationale\":\"Replace the gamma -2.5 front point with the larger-D version.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.383,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":249300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Direct comparison against C-4370b59bae5e isolates the D effect.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4370b59bae5e\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-front point between -2.5 and -3.0 at larger D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.383,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":256400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the front where the current points are 0.5 deg apart.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e6138656a3bd\",\"rationale\":\"Replace the gamma -3.0 front point with the larger-D version.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.383,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":261100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Direct D comparison against C-e6138656a3bd.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a51f1ded896c\",\"rationale\":\"Replace the gamma -3.2 front point with the larger-D version.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.383,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":265900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Direct D comparison against C-a51f1ded896c.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a51f1ded896c\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the front between gamma -3.2 and -3.45.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.383,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.35},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front at D near the mass limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-15eefd667953\",\"rationale\":\"Replace the gamma -3.45 front point with the larger-D version.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.383,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Direct D comparison against C-15eefd667953.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-c4095cf95503\",\"rationale\":\"Approach the g limit at D=3.383 from the shallow side.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.383,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.52},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Predicted g is about 11.96; it should be safely feasible and nearly at the corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3e5fe5688040\",\"rationale\":\"Corner design: D=3.383 with gamma -3.56 (predicted g about 11.985).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.383,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Aims to dominate the current corner point C-3e5fe5688040 (276350 W/m2, 391.35 K).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f579cc1dc4f8\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.384 at gamma -3.5, testing the mass-margin edge.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Predicted mass margin is about 0.0007; checks how close to the limit we can go.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3e5fe5688040\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.384 at gamma -3.54 for more coverage near the corner.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.54},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Refines the corner while staying below the g cap (predicted g about 11.96).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3e5fe5688040\",\"rationale\":\"Push to the g limit at D=3.384 (predicted g about 11.99).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.565},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the extra 0.001 m of D and the steeper gamma remain within both g and mass margins.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3e5fe5688040\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.385 at gamma -3.55, probing the mass-fraction limit (predicted margin about 0.0002).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the D limit; if feasible it is the best-D corner point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-15eefd667953\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.385 at mid-steep gamma -3.4 to fill the front and confirm the mass limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Same D probe at lower g, so any infeasibility can be attributed to mass and not to g.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3e5fe5688040\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.38, known mass margin +0.0031, at gamma -3.565 (predicted g about 11.99).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.565},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A safer point near the corner that should be feasible with certainty on mass.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3e5fe5688040\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.382 at gamma -3.565 as a hedge between 3.38 and 3.384.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.382,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.565},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fine-grained sensitivity of g and mass near the corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3e5fe5688040\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.383 at gamma -3.548, between the -3.52 and -3.565 points.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.383,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.548},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a safe corner point with about 0.03 g margin.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":134319,"type":"result","duration_ms":179283,"uuid":"e447322b-2edd-474c-88e0-0cf677ed8744","ttft_stream_ms":2224,"time_to_request_ms":132,"first_content_frame_ms":2225,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
